      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "html": "Great Lighting is Essential in producing a quality Self Tape.",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/courses/perfect-self-tape/equipment-guide/images/327b81b2-345f-4a6d-a2d1-972edc3426cf.png",
          "width": 325,
          "height": 260
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "A Simple 3-Point Lighting Set Up will do wonders for your Self Tapes.",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "The Strongest Light will be the Main Light.",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "This Main Light will be 45% from the lens of your recording device. To the right or left."
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "The second brightest will be your Fill Light.",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "A Fill Light is used to eliminate shadows on the face. This light will be powered to about 60% intensity and angled towards subject on the other side of the lens."
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "The third light...",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "A Hair Light or Backlight is often overlooked. This light will be used to separate the subject from the backdrop and really make you look like a professional. It creates depth and makes the Actor pop."
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "This light will be low intensity around 30%. And it will be fixed above or behind the subject."
        }
      ],
      "background": {
        "image": "/courses/perfect-self-tape/equipment-guide/images/f10d05d5-ff20-4d31-b747-af6dbed5ff50.jpg",
